+- `git show b7f13f4:SKILL.md | awk 'NR>=4&&NR<=18{s+=length($0)} END{print s}'` → `1037`, exit 0; `awk 'NR>=3&&NR<=8{printf "%d:%d ",NR,length($0)}'` → `3:14 4:76 5:78 6:73 7:79 8:72` (sum 392), exit 0.
+- First sentence: `git show b7f13f4:SKILL.md | python3 -c "import sys,yaml;d=yaml.safe_load(sys.stdin.read().split('---')[1])['description'].strip();print(len(d.split('. ')[0]+'.'))"` → `151`, exit 0.
+
+**Re-derivation owed by R1.** The same premise was written into `plans/round-75.md:15` ("current description frontmatter lines 4–8 lengths are 76,78,73,79,72 (the stale 1,021-char assertion in `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` is not the current base)"). No round-75 claim consumed it — round 75's C1 is the equality-threshold claim on `SKILL.md:193` — so this correction withdraws the plan's base note and the Gate reject; nothing else in round 75 rests on the number. The number is restated by the frozen counter `python3 -B verifiers/check_r75_routed_repairs.py --rev <rev>`; its receipt `.ufo/waves/round-76/receipts/r1-folded-render.txt` — filed at the round-76 path because the frozen counter reads it there — recomputes the render from the revision it names (`ac9f29510d3914a6edb97c8dbdb3445cab9141de`, the round-75 tip), prints both variants (clip 1,022 / stripped 1,021) and names the convention.
+
+**Rule.** Measure a folded block scalar by its render over the whole block at a named revision, never by a line window: `length($0)` counts the two-space indent and the `description: >` marker, and folding replaces each line break with one space. Recorded as Q74 in this round's quality-table repair (`corpus/QUALITY.md`; draft at `.ufo/waves/round-76/build/B08-q74-quality-row.diff`). Authority: `corpus/lessons/round-75-verifier-spotcheck.md` § 6 R1, with the disagreement it rests on at § 4 (`:63`) and the harmed quality trend at § 5 (`:72`).
